===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{synonym of|en|surname|nodot=a}}, a [[person]]'s [[family name]].
# The [[last]] [[element]] of a [[full name]], [[particularly]] when it could also be [[given name]] in [[East Asia]]n and other cultural traditions.
#* {{quote|1=en|2=In a structure typical for East Asia cultures, last names are usually used as given names. It usually differentiates that person from the other members of a group (typically a family or clan) who have a common family name}}

====Usage notes====
Both {{m|en|surname}} and ''last name'' are extremely common terms for family names in all dialects of English. The former is somewhat more common in the UK and the latter in the US. Because of the cultural or gendered associations involved, however, it is increasingly common to prefer {{m|en|family name}} or {{m|en|surname}} in multicultural or official contexts.

